  m_text: The<b> GJK (Gilbert-Johnson-Keerthi)</b> algorithm is an efficient method
    for determining whether two convex geometric shapes intersect (collide). It cleverly
    transforms the complex problem of geometric intersection into an iterative process
    of searching for a simple geometric entity (simplex) that encloses the origin
    within a specific space.
